# Allowlist. Everything is excluded, then exactly what the service needs is
# re-included, so a new file in the repository never silently enters the image.
*

!package.json

# The legacy core the original technical tools run on.
!dist/
dist/*
!dist/core.js

# Transports.
!server/
server/*
!server/mcp.mjs
!server/mcp-studio.mjs
!server/api.mjs
!railway/
railway/*
!railway/Dockerfile
!railway/auth.mjs
!railway/server.mjs
!railway/canonical-probe.sh

# The Canonical-aware Studio backend the Application Service orchestrates.
# Tests, fixtures, the browser app and the audio worker stay out: the service
# imports none of them.
!studio/
studio/*
!studio/backend/

# The Published Canonical bootstrap reads the Manifest and the pinned rules
# snapshot out of Git history, so the repository metadata has to be present for
# any Canonical-aware operation to run. Without it the service still starts and
# still serves capability discovery -- it reports CANONICAL_NOT_LOADED, which is
# the honest answer -- but nothing Canonical-aware will work.
!.git/
